 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Your File Explorer can do way more than you think.",
   "s": 0.06,
   "e": 2.47
  },
  {
   "text": "Here are five tricks most people never use.",
   "s": 2.89,
   "e": 5.317
  },
  {
   "text": "The last one saves the most time.",
   "s": 5.737,
   "e": 7.404
  },
  {
   "text": "First, press Windows and E to open File Explorer.",
   "s": 7.824,
   "e": 10.984
  },
  {
   "text": "Trick one: press Alt and D to jump straight to the address bar.",
   "s": 11.404,
   "e": 14.893
  },
  {
   "text": "Type any path, like C colon backslash Work, and press Enter.",
   "s": 15.313,
   "e": 18.938
  },
  {
   "text": "You're there instantly.",
   "s": 19.358,
   "e": 20.548
  },
  {
   "text": "Trick two: see what your files really are.",
   "s": 20.968,
   "e": 23.068
  },
  {
   "text": "Click View, then Show, then File name extensions.",
   "s": 23.488,
   "e": 26.384
  },
  {
   "text": "Now every file shows its real type, like dot T X T or dot P N G.",
   "s": 26.804,
   "e": 31.692
  },
  {
   "text": "That helps you spot a file pretending to be something else.",
   "s": 32.112,
   "e": 34.997
  },
  {
   "text": "Trick three: click a file and press Alt and P.",
   "s": 35.417,
   "e": 37.814
  },
  {
   "text": "The preview pane opens, so you can read it without opening it.",
   "s": 38.234,
   "e": 41.801
  },
  {
   "text": "Trick four: press Control, Shift and N.",
   "s": 42.221,
   "e": 44.156
  },
  {
   "text": "A new folder appears, ready to name.",
   "s": 44.576,
   "e": 46.508
  },
  {
   "text": "Type a name and press Enter.",
   "s": 46.928,
   "e": 48.334
  },
  {
   "text": "Trick five saves the most time.",
   "s": 48.754,
   "e": 50.325
  },
  {
   "text": "Select any file and press Alt and Enter.",
   "s": 50.745,
   "e": 52.958
  },
  {
   "text": "Its properties open right away, with the size, location and dates.",
   "s": 53.378,
   "e": 57.406
  },
  {
   "text": "Save this so you remember all five.",
   "s": 57.826,
   "e": 59.588
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow for more Windows tips.",
   "s": 60.008,
   "e": 61.484
  },
  {
   "text": "And next time you need a folder fast, start with Alt and D.",
   "s": 61.904,
   "e": 65.315
  }
 ]
}